<title>JAPAN: Japan 1996 copper cable/wire orders, shipments up.</title>
<headline>Japan 1996 copper cable/wire orders, shipments up.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese orders and shipments of copper wire and cable edged marginally higher in 1996 from the year before, the Japanese Electric Wire and Cable Makers' Association said on Friday.</p>
<p>The 1996 data was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			1996	yr/yr change</p>
<p> Orders	 1,048,928	 +1.1 pct</p>
<p>   Exports	 53,040	 -3.4 pct</p>
<p> Shipments    1,047,293	 +1.3 pct</p>
<p>   Constr'n     382,614	 +6.9 pct</p>
<p>   Electrical   277,761	 -3.7 pct</p>
<p>   Elec Power   129,666	 -4.4 pct</p>
<p>   Automobile    69,429	 +6.6 pct</p>
<p>   Telecomms     42,388	 +1.5 pct</p>
<p>   Exports	 49,971	 -9.3 pct</p>
<p>The association also said that orders for aluminium wire and cable, mostly from the electric power sector, rose 12.7 percent to 79,803 tonnes, although shipments fell 21.4 percent to 62,351 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
